&lt;p&gt;Out-of-the-box thinkers who put merit before all else. A group of ambitious and disciplined individuals who are passionate about turning theory into rubber, metal and results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; data-token-index=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt; Build the function that knows what the fleet is doing, what it will do next, and what to fix first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own fleet health: what we measure, what good looks like, and how it is reported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate fleet-wide behaviour from logs and telemetry: spot a warning appearing on a handful of robots, work out which release or configuration change introduced it, quantify how many robots are exposed and how badly, and judge the real operational severity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the fleet&#39;s diagnostic data capture — work with other teams for rosbag recording rules, log pipelines, telemetry coverage. If a failure cannot be investigated because the data was not recorded, that is a reliability defect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own alert thresholds, alert quality, resolution and escalation;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop pre-failure detection of robot subsystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own fleet configuration management: baselines, drift detection, change visibility, and driving the configuration itself towards something manageable rather than hand-tuned per robot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own fleet data quality and the hardware health foundation: component-level tracking, and a monthly fleet health report to Service and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;preventive maintenance intervals set from fleet data,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside V&amp;amp;V on release candidate analysis: interpret what RC robots are showing, catch regressions before wide rollout, and recommend proceed, hold or roll back. V&amp;amp;V owns the release decision; you supply the evidence behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the top-failure-modes register and drive the highest-impact items to resolution with Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report fleet health to the interested teams (Service, Engineering, Software).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach and grow the team; stay hands-on with data and robots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach and grow the team; stay hands-on with data and robots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial engineering experience in reliability, SRE, platform operations, robotics operations or a strongly data-driven engineering role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with telemetry and observability: Grafana or similar, time-series data, SQL, Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The analytical judgement to separate signal from noise, and to tell the difference between a robot that is unusual and a robot that is failing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough systems depth to be credible with engineers: Linux, logs, distributed systems, and ideally ROS or another robotics stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to argue a case from evidence and hold a position with engineering and hardware teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The discipline to protect proactive work from reactive pull.&lt;/li&gt;
