&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Office Manager will be responsible for helping successfully run the office space whilst supporting the senior management team with all things operations. As a progressive &amp;amp; growing start up, you will be fundamental in ensuring we have a well managed space and a fantastic environment. If you are keen on making things happen against all odds, then you are who we’re looking for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There will be a requirement to be at our office in Wallingford 5 days per week&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a senior/experienced Office Manager to oversee general operations and to ensure our offices/facilities run smoothly. You are very proactive and constantly on top of things. You easily build rapport with others. You observe and preemptively support the management team. You are passionate about growing yourself and versatile in your approach to doing. In a startup this role is broad and hands-on. One hour you might be sorting out a new starter&#39;s equipment, the next negotiating with a supplier or planning the next team offsite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Office and workplace&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the day-to-day operation of the office, including supplies, snacks, cleaning, and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the space safe, tidy, and welcoming for the team and visitors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle health and safety requirements, including fire safety checks and first aid provisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate onboarding and offboarding logistics, including equipment, accounts, desk setup, and welcome packs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan team events, socials, all-hands meetings, and company offsites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a friendly first point of contact for questions and requests from the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape and protect our culture as we grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Admin and operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records for equipment, licences, and insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arrange travel and accommodation for the team and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide occasional diary and admin support to the founders/leadership team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems and improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up and improve simple processes, checklists, and documentation as we scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with IT basics such as laptop setup, access, and coordinating with internal IT support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot problems before they happen, and suggest better ways of doing things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Previous Experience &amp;amp; Key Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 5 years in an office management position, ideally within a startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with overseeing invoicing/accounts and managing company payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with either internal or external events organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and a very high level of autonomy and accountability. You are not afraid to roll your sleeves up to make stuff happen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organisation skills and capacity to react to urgent requests&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a very fast-paced environment by efficiently managing your time and multitasking to work around other team members’ schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other key skills: exceptional time management skills, attention to detail, interpersonal skills and confidence with tools like Google Workspace or Microsoft 365, and quick to learn new software&lt;/li&gt;
