&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take your customer analysis out of the dashboard and onto the warehouse floor.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Senior Customer Analyst &lt;/strong&gt;you already know how to find the story in customer data: segments, drivers of churn, usage patterns, voice-of-customer signals. Here, you&#39;ll pair that with what you see first-hand in live warehouses, then use both to decide which product bets Dexory makes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to the &quot;why&quot; behind the numbers.&lt;/strong&gt; Run contextual inquiry, operator and manager interviews, surveys, card sorts, and prototype and usability tests across every stage of deployment and every persona.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check site behaviour against behaviour at scale.&lt;/strong&gt; Combine what you observe on site with Pendo and DexoryView usage data, so no insight rests on one warehouse or one dashboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Validate or kill ideas quickly.&lt;/strong&gt; Pressure-test concepts with A/B tests, prototype tests and interviews, and tell the team whether a bet solves a real problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close the loop after go-live.&lt;/strong&gt; Log structured operator and site-manager feedback, pass it to the PM, and keep it in the research repository.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Size the opportunity.&lt;/strong&gt; Support market sizing and competitive mapping for specific themes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn findings into decisions.&lt;/strong&gt; Write clear, presentation-ready syntheses and share them through Notion and Slack, internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the insight machinery.&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain SurveyMonkey dashboards, co-maintain the research insights pipeline, and feed capacity and progress data into the shared operating dashboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape how we work with AI.&lt;/strong&gt; Co-design the AI enablement playbook for research, covering workflows, prompts, guardrails, and what stays human-only versus human-in-the-loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Give the user a voice.&lt;/strong&gt; Co-develop UX content with the Lead and Commercial team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years in research, qual/quant insight, or product/bet design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grounding in qualitative and quantitative methods, and the judgement to know which one a question needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity, from open question through to early product bet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with tools like Notion, SurveyMonkey, Slack, Pendo and Basecamp&lt;/li&gt;
